      "m1_page": 54,
      "m1_chunk_id": "1fac7938bfb292551f02a5136c8b69a493ddff41f8a31ad3f22720dd221fe346",
      "m1_text_span": "You will know you are stepping into the realm of massive action when you (1) create new problems for yourself and (2) start to receive criticism and warning from others.",
      "m2_chunk_ids": [
        "69d46656839756687ebddd982ef16add0eff62c0d8673cfc557cae8c36e4c39e"
      ],
      "status": "exact"
    },
    {
      "question_id": "Q020",
      "evidence_type": "primary",
      "grade": 3,
      "relevance": "primary",
      "m1_page": 19,
      "m1_chunk_id": "a41219c868ab37b20f3dfd4007bf514c1a21a830a66798075da2303c7ae159dc",
      "m1_text_span": "Your focus should be on the kind of success that builds upon itself—that which is perpetual and doesn't happen only one time. This book is about how to create extraordinary achievement, how to ensure you will attain it, how to keep it—and then how to keep creating new levels of it without it feeling like work.",
      "m2_chunk_ids": [
        "374777e3295c887c9c681addbbcc5da0213b7adecff1d22b6b3840f451d8f87a"
      ],
      "status": "exact"
    },
    {
      "question_id": "Q020",
      "evidence_type": "acceptable",
      "grade": 2,
      "relevance": "acceptable",
      "m1_page": 14,
      "m1_chunk_id": "7286e2f5ea66cde5b6347e0e302a528ffbeeb1563d37e7a440aa8bf7b665156f",
      "m1_text_span": "Extremely successful people know that their efforts must continue in order for them to realize new achievements.",
      "m2_chunk_ids": [
        "eacb6c2d8137823ff4489d163ed0d185719863b6c9254d1646b5966a3d7c3397"
      ],
      "status": "exact"
    },
    {
      "question_id": "Q021",
      "evidence_type": "primary",
      "grade": 3,
      "relevance": "primary",
      "m1_page": 47,
      "m1_chunk_id": "591eed39dce448a4bdc89127ed0626632a32250c175234be9d02b01c0522bb0b",
      "m1_text_span": "The First Degree of Action “Doing nothing” is exactly what it sounds like",
      "m2_chunk_ids": [
        "45b726d888c4a93307ac1d66cb9d1e15c37c710701bba029898de709bd600aaa"
      ],
      "status": "exact"
    },
    {
      "question_id": "Q021",
      "evidence_type": "primary",
      "grade": 3,
      "relevance": "primary",
      "m1_page": 47,
      "m1_chunk_id": "c5ee746699ef341003c8af6a6e5a5467ae432ed6a196073843b65dffa2556735",
      "m1_text_span": "The Second Degree of Action“Retreaters” are those who take actions in reverse",
      "m2_chunk_ids": [
        "785b31676f422035f504c4a649c3673e38e95375c258c84d0c80f34ba6196aa0"
      ],
      "status": "manual_resolution"
    },
    {
      "question_id": "Q021",
      "evidence_type": "primary",
      "grade": 3,
      "relevance": "primary",
      "m1_page": 49,
      "m1_chunk_id": "4528f6dbcf02f811ca57e8ac8c845173430300f4ff0cba3407d6c66cf83226e8",
      "m1_text_span": "The Third Degree of Action People who take normal levels of action",
      "m2_chunk_ids": [
        "405f3d5a35c48f3e650172742c233dddd87251341fa4b0fd8a967fc06714c213"
      ],
      "status": "exact"
    },
    {
      "question_id": "Q021",
      "evidence_type": "primary",
      "grade": 3,
      "relevance": "primary",
      "m1_page": 50,
      "m1_chunk_id": "d783d5b6517982bbeab95263c5d0e880acf22e97ae0a91a6c6ada7b7ca4e06ca",
      "m1_text_span": "The Fourth Degree: Massive ActionThough it might sound far-fetched, massive action is the most natural state of action",
      "m2_chunk_ids": [
        "25b74d8908aba01a564ec4a5350d1cfbedd444d432d8d1164d022220ed73dbf1"
      ],
      "status": "manual_resolution"
    },
    {
      "question_id": "Q022",
      "evidence_type": "primary",
      "grade": 3,
      "relevance": "primary",
      "m1_page": 16,
      "m1_chunk_id": "70863271248ee1dfc643591267d859eda1ada46d35002f52d72f06befd244831",
      "m1_text_span": "You must set targets that are 10 times what you think you want and then do 10 times what you think it will take",
      "m2_chunk_ids": [
        "b9e4daec0cf3b26b214cf994276b7848cf39420947c3eb78b93437ad2ea20f7b"
      ],
      "status": "exact"
    },
    {
      "question_id": "Q023",
      "evidence_type": "primary",
      "grade": 3,
      "relevance": "primary",
      "m1_page": 49,
      "m1_chunk_id": "9eebea017b6b22d27e091df0fcfb9348aa713cd3851fde833815294bf619141e",
      "m1_text_span": "Average, by definition, assumes “less than extraordinary.”",
      "m2_chunk_ids": [
        "405f3d5a35c48f3e650172742c233dddd87251341fa4b0fd8a967fc06714c213"
      ],
      "status": "exact"
    },
